  "guide": {
    "title": "One certificate, or the whole roster",
    "tracks": [
      {
        "id": "one",
        "label": "One person",
        "steps": [
          "Pick a **Kind** - completion, achievement, award or appreciation. It writes the title, the line above what the certificate is for and the mark on the seal.",
          "Fill in the name, what it is for and the date. **Signed by** and **Their role** print above and below the signature line; leave **Signed by** empty to drop that column.",
          "**Style** sets the look and **Size** the shape. Each style takes its colours from the design system, so choosing another colourway in the sidebar recolours the certificate. A4 and US Letter export at their true physical size.",
          "To share it as a moving piece, choose a **Motion** and export MP4, WebM, GIF, APNG or animated WebP. PDF and still images always show the finished certificate."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "roster",
        "label": "A whole roster",
        "steps": [
          "Open **Bulk from rows** from the tool menu. It opens the batch grid with this tool already loaded.",
          "Import a CSV whose columns are named **firstname**, **lastname**, **awardtopic** and **awarddate**. Those are the same input ids the badge and stationery tools use, so one roster feeds all of them.",
          "Add a **language** column, such as de or ja, to print each person's certificate in their own language. Anything you leave out of the CSV keeps the value set here.",
          "Export the whole run: each row renders its own certificate, in the chosen size and format, and they come back as one zip."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
